<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bunnag family</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as House of Bunnag</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bunnag family was a noble family of Siam, descended from the Persian merchant Sheikh Ahmad who settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya</a> in the early seventeenth century. Its members held the great ministries of the Rattanakosin court for much of the nineteenth century, and Si Suriyawong governed as regent for the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chulalongkorn">Chulalongkorn</a> from 1868 to 1873, before the king curbed the family's power.</p></div>
